// src/v4/extdeps/frameworks/react.dag
//
// Scope: React framework substrate — module surface, function components,
//         elements (host + composite), props sites, ordered child refs,
//         context bindings, hook sites, effect scheduling — all declarative.
// Anchor: React **19.1.0** (npm `react@19.1.0`) — release authority
//   https://github.com/facebook/react/releases/tag/v19.1.0 . Rolling API index
//   https://react.dev/reference/react (partition + hook list C1-tracked against
//   the semver pin; site-only drift without a matching pin edit = STOP).
// Anchor: composition mental model — https://react.dev/learn
// Unifies: (per THESIS:188) framework spec = transport spec = interpreter
//         runtime where applicable. ONE substrate carrier set per React slice;
//         emit / ingest / eval read distinct facts from the same declarations —
//         extend THIS file, not parallel "emit-only" mirrors.
//
// Owns:
//   - ReactModuleSurface (client vs React Server Components module capability)
//   - ReactFunctionComponent (surface + props type/value **refs** + render root **ref**)
//   - ReactPropsSite (props type + value **refs** — call-site / element payload)
//   - ReactElement (+ host / composite / fragment / text variants) with
//     `children_refs: List<Symbol>` (A1: ordered children are **name-references**,
//     never producer-inlined subtrees at this substrate layer)
//   - ReactContextBinding (opaque `createContext` pair identity at a site)
//   - ReactHook, ReactHookKind, ReactBuiltinHook (closed hook API partition)
//   - ReactComponentEffect (trigger + **effect_body_ref** Symbol)
//   - ReactEffectTrigger (closed scheduling-class partition)
//   - Rules-of-Hooks → `std/diagnostic.dag` `Diagnostic` at consumers (lens-owned
//     `reason: Symbol` rows — not enumerated here)
//
// Consumes (traceability):
//   - std/node.dag: Node + Symbol (import **both** — the lowering closure resolves
//     `List<Symbol>` and other `Symbol` carriers only when `node.dag` is loaded;
//     `Node` stays unused in field types here but is required import-closure glue)
//   - std/collection.dag: List<T>
//   - std/diagnostic.dag: Outcome<T> ratified (DECISIONS.md **I**, #3181) —
//     referenced in commentary for future parse/resolve seams; no operation rows
//     authored here yet (DECLARATIVE-NOW).
//   - extdeps/languages/typescript.dag: props / element-type facts resolve through
//     TS name table (traceability — no `import` until a shared carrier requires it)
//
// Owned ELSEWHERE (named triggers unchanged in intent):
//   - JSX/TSX grammar, synthetic events, portals, Suspense, error boundaries —
//     T-4 LanguageModel / emit lanes
//   - Class components — grammar layer
//   - Next.js `"use client"` spelling — adjacent framework extdeps if ratified
//   - Per-hook algebra inhabitance, D2 resolver numeric rows, GroundingMap home —
//     operator-pinned homes (#3195 / #3200 discipline); never mint parallel std/
//   - `parse_* / lower_* -> Outcome<…>` operation realizations — compiler stages
//     once B2-OMNI wires hook sites to outcomes (D1 landed in std/diagnostic.dag)
//
// Status: T-4.7 forward-modeled — DOC-ANCHOR per carrier; A1 child refs; C5 partition.
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md; splitting requires operator ratification (substrate
// extension = stop signal).


module v4.extdeps.frameworks.react


import v4.std.node { Node, Symbol }
import v4.std.collection { List }


// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Modeling notes
//
// SYMBOL-REF DISCIPLINE (A1 + K-1). Every `*_ref` field is an opaque `Symbol`
// resolved through the module / component namespace to a declaration or value
// site authored in the TS+React grammar layer — the React substrate does not
// carry inlined `Node` forests for children, custom hooks, or effect bodies here.
// `Node` remains the kernel's sole recursive program carrier (node.dag A1);
// React graphs **attach** to it by reference, not by embedding another recursion.
//
// D1/D2. Fail-closed stage returns use `Outcome<T>` from `v4.std.diagnostic` when
// operations land; this file declares **data** carriers only (DECLARATIVE-NOW).
//
// C5 / #3200. Coproduct ledgers below are 🟢 terminal classifiers over React's
// documented API partitions for the pin; any future richer source that would
// duplicate authority without collapsing here ⇒ 🟡 + operator trigger (not
// improvised in-lane).


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactModuleSurface
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/rsc/server-components (RSC surface) +
//         https://react.dev/reference/react/use-client (client module boundary;
//         directive mechanics Owned ELSEWHERE — this enum is the **capability**
//         tag consumers read once the boundary parser has fired)
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: coordination + emit read one module-surface tag.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: `{ is_server: Bool }` admits illegal merged state.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: module capability boundary, not an algebra carrier.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: exactly one surface tag per modeled module authority.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not `F<X>` over an external enumerable; two
//      named React-19 module stories only.
// Terminal: closed binary module-capability partition (React 19.1.0 docs).
type ReactModuleSurface
  = ReactClientModule
  | ReactServerComponentsModule


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactBuiltinHook
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react/hooks (index) — each variant names
//         one stable `react@19.1.0` export (`useState` … `use`); verify against
//         https://github.com/facebook/react/releases/tag/v19.1.0 on API churn.
//
// ORDERING: react.dev Hooks reference left-nav order for mechanical audit diffs.
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: shared resolver/emit discriminator for all hooks.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: Int `hook_id` admits out-of-range illegal hooks.
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: per-hook algebras inhabit std/ elsewhere — this
//      sum stays the API partition, not a collapse into one algebra.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: one built-in hook kind per call site — exclusive tags.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not Practice-7 mechanical copy; eighteen named
//      API surfaces.
// Terminal: closed eighteen-way `react` package hook classifier (React 19.1.0).
type ReactBuiltinHook
  = ReactUseState
  | ReactUseReducer
  | ReactUseContext
  | ReactUseRef
  | ReactUseImperativeHandle
  | ReactUseEffect
  | ReactUseLayoutEffect
  | ReactUseInsertionEffect
  | ReactUseMemo
  | ReactUseCallback
  | ReactUseTransition
  | ReactUseDeferredValue
  | ReactUseId
  | ReactUseSyncExternalStore
  | ReactUseDebugValue
  | ReactUseActionState
  | ReactUseOptimistic
  | ReactUseApi


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactHookKind
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/rules/rules-of-hooks (custom = composition
//         of hooks; built-ins = finite API table above)
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: one discriminant for expansion vs custom composition.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: `{ is_builtin: Bool, impl_ref: Symbol }` admits
//      builtin+arbitrary impl simultaneously — contradicts Rules of Hooks partition.
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: custom resolves to a referenced declaration body
//      (hooks composed only inside that body — grammar proof obligation ELSEWHERE).
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: built-in XOR custom at one site — not coordinates.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: heterogeneous payloads (`ReactBuiltinHook` vs
//      `Symbol`) — not uniform `F<X>`.
// Terminal: built-in vs custom-hook **reference** partition.
type ReactHookKind
  = Builtin { hook: ReactBuiltinHook }
  | Custom { implementation_ref: Symbol }


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactHook
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react/hooks + dependency-array semantics per
//         hook family (e.g. https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect#parameters )
//
// `dependency_value_refs`: ordered dependency expressions; each `Symbol` names a
// value site (including "absent array" modeled as empty list at grammar policy).
// A1: refs, not inlined expression `Node`s at this layer.
type ReactHook {
  kind: ReactHookKind
  dependency_value_refs: List<Symbol>
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactEffectTrigger
// Anchor: https://react.dev/learn/synchronizing-with-effects +
//         https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect (commit vs cleanup timing)
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: scheduling lenses read trigger uniformly.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: Int phase bitfield admits illegal combinations.
//   3. Algebraic form — N/A: reconciler obligation classes, not std/ algebra.
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: one trigger class per modeled obligation edge.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: not indexed mechanical copy of another enum.
// Terminal: closed four-way structural trigger partition (TASKS.md T-4.7).
type ReactEffectTrigger
  = Mount
  | Unmount
  | DependencyChange
  | EveryRender


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactComponentEffect
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect
//
// `effect_body_ref` names the effect function / closure declaration (cleanup
// returned inside that body — grammar encoding ELSEWHERE). A1: ref, not inlined
// `Node` subtree at this React extdeps layer.
type ReactComponentEffect {
  trigger: ReactEffectTrigger
  effect_body_ref: Symbol
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactPropsSite
// Anchor: https://react.dev/learn/passing-props-to-a-component
//
// Props are a TypeScript-shaped fact: static typing via `props_type_ref`; the
// particular props **value** at a call/element site is a separate named value
// site `props_value_ref` (K-1 opaque; spelling never read in kernel logic).
type ReactPropsSite {
  props_type_ref: Symbol
  props_value_ref: Symbol
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactFunctionComponent
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react/function-components
//
// `render_root_ref` names the root **element** declaration for this component's
// return tree (children under that root use `children_refs` inside `ReactElement`
// carriers — A1 ref spine, not inlined trees).
type ReactFunctionComponent {
  surface: ReactModuleSurface
  props: ReactPropsSite
  render_root_ref: Symbol
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactHostElement
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react-dom/components (intrinsic / host tree)
//
// Host (intrinsic) element: tag identity + props payload + ordered child **refs**.
type ReactHostElement {
  tag_ref: Symbol
  props: ReactPropsSite
  children_refs: List<Symbol>
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactCompositeElement
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react/createElement + function-components link
//
// Composite element: component **reference** + props + ordered child **refs**
// (includes `children` prop encoding — grammar decides prop vs explicit child list;
// this substrate carries the unified ordered ref spine React reconciles).
type ReactCompositeElement {
  component_ref: Symbol
  props: ReactPropsSite
  children_refs: List<Symbol>
}


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactElement
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react/createElement +
//         https://react.dev/reference/react/Fragment +
//         https://react.dev/reference/react-dom/components (host children)
//
// Coproduct dissolution (Practice 4 / modeling-discipline.md §4) —
// classification: 🟢 GREEN (terminal). Ledger — five patterns attempted:
//   1. Fact placement — FAILS: reconciler + emit share one element-shape tag.
//   2. Variant-is-data — FAILS: flat `{ kind: Int, … }` admits impossible unions
//      (host+composite payloads simultaneously).
//   3. Algebraic form — PARTIAL: host vs composite share props+children discipline
//      but differ on tag vs component ref — kept as distinct variants, not one
//      overloaded record (P2 illegal-states-unrepresentable).
//   4. Dimensional — FAILS: a value is exactly one element kind at this layer.
//   5. Parameterized family — FAILS: text vs fragment vs host vs composite are not
//      `Element<Width>` style mechanical copies (Practice 7).
// Terminal: React-reconciler element partition at the pinned major/minor.
type ReactElement
  = Host { host: ReactHostElement }
  | Composite { composite: ReactCompositeElement }
  | Fragment { children_refs: List<Symbol> }
  | Text { text_value_ref: Symbol }


// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ReactContextBinding
// Anchor: https://react.dev/reference/react/createContext +
//         https://react.dev/learn/passing-data-deeply-with-context
//
// Opaque identity for a `createContext` pair at a declaration site; Provider /
// Consumer wiring + `useContext` operand refs resolve through grammar to this
// `context_pair_ref` (K-1 — no readable context "name" in kernel logic).
type ReactContextBinding {
  context_pair_ref: Symbol
}
